    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00006",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00333:title:sect-00006-title",
        "text": "Steps 1–2 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Acyl Transfers"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00001",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00333:title:sect-00001-title",
            "text": "MECHANISM"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00004",
              "segmentId": "m00333:para:para-00004"
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00005",
              "segmentId": "m00333:para:para-00005"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00001",
              "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
              "caption": {
                "segmentId": "m00333:caption:fig-00001-caption"
              },
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00333:alt:fig-00001-alt",
                  "text": "Fatty acid biosynthesis of butyryl A C P from acetyl-coenzyme A involves a series of trans-esterifications, Claisain-like condensations, ketone reduction, dehydration, and double bond reduction."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_04_001.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00002",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00333:alt:fig-00002-alt",
                  "text": "Acetyl-coenzyme A reacts with base and H S A C P to form tetrahedral intermediate that further forms acetyl S A C P. The abbreviated mechanism is indicated in parentheses."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_04_002.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00006",
              "segmentId": "m00333:para:para-00006"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00003",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00333:alt:fig-00003-alt",
                  "text": "The structure of acetyl A C P comprises a C H 3 C O linked to phosphopantetheine and an O connected to methylene linked to serine and A C P."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_04_003.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00007",
              "segmentId": "m00333:para:para-00007"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00002",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00333:title:sect-00002-title",
            "text": "Steps 3–4 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Carboxylation and Acyl Transfer"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00008",
              "segmentId": "m00333:para:para-00008"
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00009",
              "segmentId": "m00333:para:para-00009"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00004",
              "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
              "caption": {
                "segmentId": "m00333:caption:fig-00004-caption"
              },
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00333:alt:fig-00004-alt",
                  "text": "The enzyme deprotonates acetyl-coenzyme A to form an enolate and N-carboxybiotin undergoes decarboxylation to carbon dioxide and biotin. The enolate reacts with carbon dioxide to form malonyl-coenzyme A."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_04_004.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00010",
              "segmentId": "m00333:para:para-00010"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00003",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00333:title:sect-00003-title",
            "text": "Step 5 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Condensation"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00011",
              "segmentId": "m00333:para:para-00011"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00005",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00333:alt:fig-00005-alt",
                  "text": "Acetyl synthase reacts with malonyl A C P to form an tetrahedral intermediate and carbon dioxide. This leads to acetoacetyl A C P and synthase connected to a sulfur anion."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_04_005.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00004",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00333:title:sect-00004-title",
            "text": "Steps 6–8 of [[xref:fig-00001]]: Reduction and Dehydration"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00012",
              "segmentId": "m00333:para:para-00012"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00006",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00333:alt:fig-00006-alt",
                  "text": "Acetoacetyl A C P reacts with nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate hydride to form beta-hydroxybutyrate A C P and nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate cation."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_04_006.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00013",
              "segmentId": "m00333:para:para-00013"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00007",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00333:alt:fig-00007-alt",
                  "text": "Crotonyl A C P reacts with nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide phosphate hydride to form an enolate that is protonated  to butyryl A C P."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_04_007.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00014",
              "segmentId": "m00333:para:para-00014"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00008",
              "class": "unnumbered",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00333:alt:fig-00008-alt",
                  "text": "A thiol butyryl ester undergoes condensation with HS-Synthase to form butyryl synthase. It forms a six-carbon chain linked to S A C P that further forms sixteen-carbon chain named palmitoyl A C P."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_04_008.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00015",
              "segmentId": "m00333:para:para-00015"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
